Rules:

- There is a lost-sales inventory system. Receipts (incoming shipments) add quantity to stock. Demands consume min(stock, quantity). If demand quantity > stock, the unmet portion is lost. Lost quantity is counted as lost. A stockout is strictly when there is unmet demand (i.e., demand > stock) for that event.

- For raw report histories: we keep reports where received_time <= knowledge_cutoff. Then we choose the highest visible revision for each event_id (the highest revision among those visible). Revisions replace earlier reports, not add.

- Then keep chosen events with event_time <= target_time. So we ignore events whose event_time is beyond target_time for the historical reconstruction.

- Apply these events in order sorted by (event_time, event_id) (so tie-breaking by event_id) from initial_stock.

- Important: It's possible that some event might have a received_time after knowledge_cutoff, but its event_time <= target_time. It is invisible, so we disregard it entirely, even if it occurred earlier. So the historical reconstruction only uses events that are visible (i.e., its latest revision is visible). So this may cause missing events relative to true timeline, but we only use visible ones.

